 "voice": "en-US-AvaNeural",
 "text": "Three Bright Futures mistakes Florida parents make. Number one: thinking it's automatic. It's not. Your student has to apply through the Florida Financial Aid Application, the F F A A, by August thirty-first after graduation. Number two: waiting until senior year to log service hours. Hours are earned during high school, so start a signed log in ninth grade and turn hours in every year. Number three: using the wrong G P A. Bright Futures uses its own weighted G P A, so ask the school counselor for your student's Bright Futures G P A. Want to know if your student is on track? Try our free Bright Futures checker. It's at the link in bio. And follow for more Florida college tips.",
